## Preserve exactly

- Layout and visual hierarchy (hero, KPIs, birthdays/anniversaries, search, filters, sorting, table, mobile cards, pagination)
- Crystal/glass surfaces, colors, glows, typography, icons, avatars, spacing, and animations
- Loading, empty, and error states
- Add / Edit Client modal, View Client details and booking history, Delete/Archive dialog
- Existing Clients functionality, API calls, validation, permissions, routes, and data behavior

## Other work must stay independent

Work on Login, Dashboard, Bookings, and other modules without touching the files above.

If you must change shared CSS or layout shells:

- Do not alter `.dhara-clients`, `.dhara-clients-*`, or `clients-page.css`.
- Scope new styles so they cannot override Clients descendants.
- Prefer new class names over changing globals used by Clients.

`ClientSearchSelect` and `clients-service` are consumed by other modules. Other modules may *call* them, but must not edit those locked files without explicit Clients Management approval.

## Allowed exception

Only modify the Clients Management module when the user clearly asks for a specific Clients change in that conversation.

Do not weaken `.cursor/rules/locked-login-page.mdc` or `.cursor/rules/locked-dashboard.mdc`.
